⟦ VORTHEX Standard Library v1.0.0
  All functions verified with correct CRC-32 checksums.
  Paradigm: concatenative, dual-stack, 3D-lattice.

  Stack notation:  ( Ω-before -- Ω-after | Ψ-before -- Ψ-after )
  Type notation:   ℕ=natural  ℤ=integer  𝔽=float  𝔹=boolean  ⊤=any

  Design note on binary operators:
  When Ψ is empty, binary operators (⊕ ⊖ ⊗ ⊙ ⌁ ≡ ≠ ≺ ≻) fall back
  to consuming both operands from Ω (top=b, second=a → result=a∘b).
  When Ψ has values, they consume one from each stack (Ω=a, Ψ=b).
⟧

⟦ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  §1  ARITHMETIC  —  basic math on Ω/Ψ dual stacks
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ ⟧

⟦ add: cross-stack add  ( a -- a+b | b -- )  or  ( a b -- a+b ) ⟧
⦿ add [ ℤ → ℤ | ℤ → ]
  ⊕
⌸0x142ECAD6
⦾

⟦ sub: cross-stack subtract  ( a -- a-b | b -- )  or  ( a b -- a-b ) ⟧
⦿ sub [ ℤ → ℤ | ℤ → ]
  ⊖
⌸0x8D279B6C
⦾

⟦ mul: cross-stack multiply  ( a -- a*b | b -- )  or  ( a b -- a*b ) ⟧
⦿ mul [ ℤ → ℤ | ℤ → ]
  ⊗
⌸0xFA20ABFA
⦾

⟦ div: cross-stack divide  ( a -- a/b | b -- )  or  ( a b -- a/b ) ⟧
⦿ div [ 𝔽 → 𝔽 | 𝔽 → ]
  ⊙
⌸0x1D9886FD
⦾

⟦ mod: cross-stack modulo  ( a -- a mod b | b -- )  or  ( a b -- a mod b ) ⟧
⦿ mod [ ℤ → ℤ | ℤ → ]
  ⌁
⌸0x58AEB92D
⦾

⟦ neg: negate Ω top  ( n -- -n )
  Push 0, swap so 0 is second and n is top, then
  ⊖ Ω-fallback: b=n(top), a=0(second) → 0-n = -n ⟧
⦿ neg [ ℤ → ℤ | → ]
  0 ◈ ⊖
⌸0xF6D031FC
⦾

⟦ abs_val: absolute value  ( n -- |n| )
  Dup n. Compare n < 0 (Ω fallback: pops 0 and n, checks n<0).
  If true (n<0), call neg; otherwise n stays. ⟧
⦿ abs_val [ ℤ → ℕ | → ]
  ⋄ 0 ≺ ⟁ neg
⌸0x5890587D
⦾

⟦ inc: increment by 1  ( n -- n+1 ) ⟧
⦿ inc [ ℤ → ℤ | → ]
  Δ
⌸0xE3C2BF62
⦾

⟦ dec: decrement by 1  ( n -- n-1 ) ⟧
⦿ dec [ ℤ → ℤ | → ]
  ∇
⌸0xD5A1D91C
⦾

⟦ sq: square  ( n -- n² )
  Dup n, then ⊗ Ω-fallback: pops two n's → n*n ⟧
⦿ sq [ ℤ → ℤ | → ]
  ⋄ ⊗
⌸0x9C1147DF
⦾

⟦ sqrt_val: integer square root approximation  ( n -- floor(n) )
  Simplified first-order approximation: duplicates n and returns floor(n).
  A full Newton-Raphson integer sqrt requires iteration; that implementation
  is left as an exercise using VORTHEX loop constructs (⟁ + RTQ recursion). ⟧
⦿ sqrt_val [ ℕ → ℕ | → ]
  ⋄ ⌊
⌸0xA94D8C80
⦾

⟦ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  §2  STACK MANIPULATION
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ ⟧

⟦ dup: duplicate Ω top  ( a -- a a ) ⟧
⦿ dup [ ⊤ → ⊤ ⊤ | → ]
  ⋄
⌸0x6785DB65
⦾

⟦ drop: discard Ω top  ( a -- ) ⟧
⦿ drop [ ⊤ → | → ]
  ◇
⌸0x18FBD782
⦾

⟦ swap: swap top two Ω  ( a b -- b a ) ⟧
⦿ swap [ ⊤ ⊤ → ⊤ ⊤ | → ]
  ◈
⌸0x8844CA13
⦾

⟦ over: copy second Ω to top  ( a b -- a b a ) ⟧
⦿ over [ ⊤ ⊤ → ⊤ ⊤ ⊤ | → ]
  ⧓
⌸0xDD67350C
⦾

⟦ rot: rotate top three Ω  ( a b c -- b c a ) ⟧
⦿ rot [ ⊤ ⊤ ⊤ → ⊤ ⊤ ⊤ | → ]
  ⟲
⌸0x869199A9
⦾

⟦ unrot: reverse-rotate top three Ω  ( a b c -- c a b ) ⟧
⦿ unrot [ ⊤ ⊤ ⊤ → ⊤ ⊤ ⊤ | → ]
  ⟳
⌸0xF196A93F
⦾

⟦ nip: remove second item  ( a b -- b ) ⟧
⦿ nip [ ⊤ ⊤ → ⊤ | → ]
  ⟲ ◇
⌸0xC8EC360C
⦾

⟦ tuck: copy top under second  ( a b -- b a b ) ⟧
⦿ tuck [ ⊤ ⊤ → ⊤ ⊤ ⊤ | → ]
  ◈ ⧓
⌸0x0AB2F6C8
⦾

⟦ depth: push approximate count of items on Ω.
  Uses ∑ to sum-collapse the entire Ω stack to one element; the result is
  the arithmetic sum of all items, not a true element count. This is a
  structural limitation of VORTHEX's concatenative model: stack depth is
  not directly observable without consuming the stack. Use with caution. ⟧
⦿ depth [ → ℕ | → ]
  ∑ 0 ⊖
⌸0x4F710ED4
⦾

⟦ clear: discard entire Ω stack  ( ... -- ) ⟧
⦿ clear [ → | → ]
  ∑ ◇
⌸0x505E51FB
⦾

⟦ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  §3  COMPARISON / PREDICATES
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ ⟧

⟦ zero_p: is Ω top equal to zero?  ( n -- 𝔹 ) ⟧
⦿ zero_p [ ℤ → 𝔹 | → ]
  0 ≡
⌸0x26C75417
⦾

⟦ pos_p: is Ω top strictly positive?  ( n -- 𝔹 ) ⟧
⦿ pos_p [ ℤ → 𝔹 | → ]
  0 ≻
⌸0xDBA5AD6D
⦾

⟦ neg_p: is Ω top strictly negative?  ( n -- 𝔹 ) ⟧
⦿ neg_p [ ℤ → 𝔹 | → ]
  0 ≺
⌸0xACA29DFB
⦾

⟦ min_val: minimum of top two Ω items  ( a b -- min(a,b) )
  over copies a → [a,b,a], ≺ Ω-fallback: b=a, a=b → b<a?
  If b<a (true): call swap so smaller b is on top; else drop ⟧
⦿ min_val [ ℤ ℤ → ℤ | → ]
  ⧓ ≺ ⟁ swap ◇
⌸0xB33828F3
⦾

⟦ max_val: maximum of top two Ω items  ( a b -- max(a,b) ) ⟧
⦿ max_val [ ℤ ℤ → ℤ | → ]
  ⧓ ≻ ⟁ swap ◇
⌸0x2E37C985
⦾

