⟦ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  §7  LATTICE OPERATIONS
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ ⟧

⟦ lat_copy: read/write lattice cell using entropy Z-coordinate
  Ω-mode: write Ω top to ℒ[Ω[-2]][Ψ top][ε & 0xFF]
  Ψ-mode: read from same coordinates → Ω ⟧
⦿ lat_copy [ ℕ → ⊤ | ℕ → ]
  ⊘
⌸0x6A9FB66B
⦾

⟦ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  §8  RECURSIVE ALGORITHMS
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ ⟧

⟦ fib: Fibonacci  ( n -- fib(n) )
  fib(0)=0, fib(1)=1.  For n > 1: delegates to fib_recurse.
  ⋄ 1 ≻: dup n, push 1, ≻ Ω-fallback → (n > 1)?
  ⟁ fib_recurse: if n>1, call fib_recurse; else return n unchanged. ⟧
⦿ fib [ ℕ → ℕ | → ]
  ⋄ 1 ≻ ⟁ fib_recurse
⌸0xE6588286
⦾

⟦ fib_recurse: computes fib(n) = fib(n-1) + fib(n-2) for n > 1 ⟧
⦿ fib_recurse [ ℕ → ℕ | → ]
  ⋄ ∇ fib ◈ ∇ ∇ fib ⊕
⌸0x9F4546BC
⦾

⟦ fact: Factorial  ( n -- n! )
  fact(0)=1.  For n > 0: ⋄ 0 ≻ ⟁ fact_recurse. ⟧
⦿ fact [ ℕ → ℕ | → ]
  ⋄ 0 ≻ ⟁ fact_recurse
⌸0xD01445A9
⦾

⟦ fact_recurse: computes n * fact(n-1) for n > 0 ⟧
⦿ fact_recurse [ ℕ → ℕ | → ]
  ⋄ ∇ fact ⊗
⌸0x44F5A23A
⦾

⟦ pow_int: integer exponentiation  ( base exp -- base^exp )
  Both operands on Ω: base below exp on top.
  pow(base, 0) = 1; pow(base, n) = base * pow(base, n-1). ⟧
⦿ pow_int [ ℕ → ℕ | → ]
  ⊃ 0 ≡ ⟁ pow_base
  ⊃ ⋄ ∇ ⊂ pow_int ⊗
⌸0x46BEAC90
⦾

⟦ pow_base: base case for pow_int — n^0 = 1  ( base 0 -- 1 ) ⟧
⦿ pow_base [ ℕ → ℕ | → ]
  ◇ ◇ 1
⌸0xCF32B55E
⦾

⟦ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  §9  TYPE VALIDATION  (self-referential)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ ⟧

⟦ is_natural: type validator — returns 𝔹 on Ω  ( n -- 𝔹 )
  Returns ⊤ if Ω top is a natural number (n is integer AND n >= 0).
  Uses ≺ Ω-fallback: ⋄ ∅ ≺ pushes (n < 0), ¬ negates → (n >= 0).
  Then ∧ combines with integer check. ⟧
⦿ is_natural [ ⊤ → 𝔹 | → ]
  ⋄ ⌊ ≡ ⋄ ∅ ≺ ¬ ∧
⌸0x9D4DB97A
⦾

⟦ is_zero: type validator — returns 𝔹 on Ω  ( n -- 𝔹 ) ⟧
⦿ is_zero [ ⊤ → 𝔹 | → ]
  0 ≡
⌸0x26C75417
⦾

⟦ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  §10  REVERSE-TIME SORT DEMONSTRATION
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ ⟧

⟦ rtq_sort_demo: demonstration of RTQ (reverse-time queue) mechanics.
  Three values are pushed with ⊂ (copy to Ψ), then ⊃ moves them
  from Ψ to Ω. The RTQ feature is demonstrated externally by using
  1 blank line before statements in top-level code. ⟧
⦿ rtq_sort_demo [ → ℤ ℤ ℤ | → ]
  1 ⊂ 2 ⊂ 3 ⊂
  ⊃ ⊃ ⊃
⌸0xC47B2401
⦾

⟦ END OF VORTHEX STANDARD LIBRARY ⟧
